{"text": "Museums have their origins, both materially and conceptually, in the collections of the wealthy and the privileged. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Historically, they displayed the wealth of the collector, but also his cognitive power. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The acquisition and display of beautiful, curious, or rare objects in the Renaissance confirmed the collectors access to the secrets of the universe contained in those objects, which mediated between the visible and the invisible, the material world and the order that underlay it. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The collection indexed its proprietors access to this domain of hidden meaning and placed outsiders who were granted access to the collections in an inferior position. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Paying their respects to the collection, they acknowledged the status of the collector. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Although the evolution of the collection into the museum during the early modern period occurs along with a series of epistemic shifts in the structure of knowledge, museums remain fundamentally concerned with expressing the relationship of knowledge and ownership to identity, power, and status.", "alignment": {"characters": ["M", "u", "s", "e", "u", "m", "s", " ", "h", "a", "v", "e", " ", "t", "h", "e", "i", "r", " ", "o", "r", "i", "g", "i", "n", "s", ",", " ", "b", "o", "t", "h", " ", "m", "a", "t", "e", "r", "i", "a", "l", "l", "y", " ", "a", "n", "d", " ", "c", "o", "n", "c", "e", "p", "t", "u", "a", "l", "l", "y", ",", " ", "i", "n", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "c", "o", "l", "l", "e", "c", "t", "i", "o", "n", "s", " ", "o", "f", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "w", "e", "a", "l", "t", "h", "y", " ", "a", "n", "d", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "p", "r", "i", "v", "i", "l", "e", "g", "e", "d", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", "t", "i", "m", "e", "=", "\"", "0", ".", "8", "s", "\"", " ", "/", ">", " ", "H", "i", "s", "t", "o", "r", "i", "c", "a", "l", "l", "y", ",", " ", "t", "h", "e", "y", " ", "d", "i", "s"